    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "claude/elegant-ritchie-5b81ka",
    "head_commit_message": "feat(formation): the Rust backend owns the entries' keys\n\nSpec 35 step 2b (Decision 142). The native unit store's columns all live\non the BodyField: the store's columns move out of field.rs into\ncolumns.rs, which now holds the loose and fleeing entries' keys too, by\ntype (points, 32- and 64-bit ints, floats), each blank as UnitColumns'\nBLANKS say. BodyField's flags-only calls give way to one set per type\n(column_ints, commit_longs, int_of, put_real and the rest), and\nUnitColumnsNative holds nothing in GDScript.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KNhteRASKu7RPFwLaQZi26",
